From 29d2468857be4de1644ca4470c2a4aa7f8137656 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: junpenglao <junpenglao@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 08:06:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Report controller evidence without global certification

Finding: Metric escalation, observed ensemble disagreement, and global exploration were conflated in the public verdict; the historical route latch could certify mode coverage independently of later deferral, and a between-means route can legally coexist with a later population handoff.

Fix: remove positive coverage certification, report historical route selection, current disagreement, metric scope, exploration status, and handoff separately, correct the T-statistic and R-hat documentation, and add real coexistence regressions without changing controller gates or sampler arithmetic.

